{"name":"Spicy Cayenne","hex":"#9b5b4f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spicy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, pertaining to, or containing spice.","Of a flavor, provoking a burning sensation due to the presence of capsaicin or a similar chemical."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spicy"},{"term":"cayenne","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Ellipsis of cayenne pepper.","Spice or verve."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cayenne"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pungency","blocks":[{"text":"Pungency, commonly referred to as spiciness, hotness or heat, is a sensation that contributes to the flavor of certain foods such as chili peppers. Highly pungent foods may be experienced as unpleasant. The term piquancy is sometimes applied to foods with a lower degree of pungency that are \"agreeably stimulating to the palate\". In addition to chili peppers, piquant ingredients include wasabi, horseradish and mustard. The primary substances responsible for pungency are capsaicin, piperine and allyl isothiocyanate."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/PepperswithscovilleCentralMarketHoustonTX.JPG/330px-PepperswithscovilleCentralMarketHoustonTX.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pungency","wikidata":"Q1517948"},{"title":"Cayenne","blocks":[{"text":"Cayenne is the capital, prefecture, and largest city of French Guiana, an overseas region and department of France located in South America. The city stands on a former island at the mouth of the Cayenne River on the Atlantic coast. The city's motto is \"fert aurum industria\", which means \"work brings wealth\". Cayenne is the largest Francophone city of the South American continent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Cayenne_place_des_palmistes_rue_de_Remire_2013.jpg/330px-Cayenne_place_des_palmistes_rue_de_Remire_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cayenne","wikidata":"Q44401"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Epice_marche_Pointe_a_Pitre.JPG/500px-Epice_marche_Pointe_a_Pitre.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Epice_marche_Pointe_a_Pitre.JPG/1280px-Epice_marche_Pointe_a_Pitre.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Epice_marche_Pointe_a_Pitre.JPG/500px-Epice_marche_Pointe_a_Pitre.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A display of spices in Guadeloupe: some pungent, some not","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEpice_marche_Pointe_a_Pitre.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Cayenne_Banque_fran%C3%A7aise_commerciale_place_des_palmistes_2013.jpg/500px-Cayenne_Banque_fran%C3%A7aise_commerciale_place_des_palmistes_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Cayenne_Banque_fran%C3%A7aise_commerciale_place_des_palmistes_2013.jpg/1280px-Cayenne_Banque_fran%C3%A7aise_commerciale_place_des_palmistes_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Cayenne_Banque_fran%C3%A7aise_commerciale_place_des_palmistes_2013.jpg/500px-Cayenne_Banque_fran%C3%A7aise_commerciale_place_des_palmistes_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACayenne_Banque_fran%C3%A7aise_commerciale_place_des_palmistes_2013.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Cayenne_Anse_de_Montabo_2013.jpg/